e Unit 17 holds 992 parts.\n\nA third distinct cycle begins at Record Q00154. Unit 17 (in this context, likely a different physical location or a reset of the unit numbering scheme for a new batch) holds only 8 parts. The subsequent units again follow the +13 increment pattern (Unit 18 holds 21, Unit 19 holds 34, etc.). This cycle continues through Record Q00230, where Unit 93 holds 996 parts.\n\nFinally, the last few records (Q00231-Q00233) show a reset again. Unit 94 holds 12 parts, Unit 95 holds 25 parts, and Unit 96 holds 38 parts. This indicates that the warehouse system operates in cycles or batches, with unit numbers resetting or being reused for new inventory lots, and part counts", "last_prefill_ms": 5619, "token_events": 512, "samp_presence_penalty": 0, "grammar_resamples": 0, "total_ms": 22367, "prefill_ms": 10583, "samp_repeat_penalty": 1, "prefill_ms_per_token": 1.320893659510734, "decode_ms": 11604, "grammar_bytes": 0, "call_id": "80a349d66305da27361fae4d7d346f79", "stage": ""}
